{"id":"mahabharata-13-061","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":61,"title":"एकषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 61 · What is the best thing to give?","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira says that the scriptures tell men to give this and that, and asks what is the best of all gifts. Bhishma says that the gift of a cow is the greatest, for cows are the support of all that lives, and that one who gives the whole earth won by weapons wins fame as long as the cow lives.","kn":"ಇದನ್ನು ಕೊಡು, ಅದನ್ನು ಕೊಡು ಎಂದು ಶ್ರುತಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತದೆ, ಎಲ್ಲ ದಾನಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಉತ್ತಮವಾದುದು ಯಾವುದೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಗೋದಾನ ಶ್ರೇಷ್ಠ, ಗೋವುಗಳು ಎಲ್ಲ ಜೀವಿಗಳ ಆಧಾರ, ಶಸ್ತ್ರದಿಂದ ಗೆದ್ದ ಭೂಮಿ ನೀಡುವವನು ಗೋ ಬದುಕಿರುವವರೆಗೆ ಕೀರ್ತಿ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ ಎಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर कहते हैं कि श्रुति यह दो वह दो कहती है और पूछते हैं कि सब दानों में उत्तम क्या है। भीष्म कहते हैं कि गोदान सबसे बड़ा है क्योंकि गौएँ सब प्राणियों का आधार हैं, और शस्त्र से जीती पृथ्वी दान करने वाले की कीर्ति जब तक गौ जीवित है तब तक रहती है।","te":"ఇది ఇవ్వు, అది ఇవ్వు అని శ్రుతి చెబుతోందని, అన్ని దానాలలో ఉత్తమమైనది ఏదని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. గోదానం గొప్పదని, ఆవులు అన్ని జీవులకు ఆధారమని, శస్త్రంతో గెలిచిన భూమిని దానం చేసినవాడు ఆవు ఉన్నంత కాలం కీర్తి పొందుతాడని భీష్ముడు అంటాడు.","ta":"இதைக் கொடு, அதைக் கொடு என்று வேதம் கூறுகிறது, எல்லா தானங்களிலும் சிறந்தது எது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, பசுதானமே பெரியது, பசுக்கள் எல்லா உயிர்களின் ஆதாரம், ஆயுதத்தால் வென்ற நிலத்தைத் தருபவன் பசு உள்ளவரை புகழ் பெறுவான் என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ഇത് കൊടുക്കണം, അത് കൊടുക്കണം എന്ന് ശാസ്ത്രങ്ങൾ മനുഷ്യരോട് പറയുന്നുവെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പറയുന്നു; സകല ദാനങ്ങളിലും ഏറ്റവും മികച്ചത് ഏതെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം ചോദിക്കുന്നു. പശുദാനമാണ് ഏറ്റവും വലുതെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; ജീവിക്കുന്നവയുടെയെല്ലാം ആധാരമാണ് പശുക്കൾ. ആയുധബലത്താൽ നേടിയ ഭൂമി മുഴുവൻ ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നവൻ പശു ജീവിച്ചിരിക്കുന്ന കാലത്തോളം കീർത്തി നേടുമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.61; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"इदं देयमिदं देयमितीयं श्रुतिचोदना ।\nबहुदेयाश्च राजानः किं स्विद्देयमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Vedic command is 'give this, give that.' Kings have much to give; what, then, is the best gift?\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"अति दानानि सर्वाणि पृथिवीदानमुच्यते ।\nअचला ह्यक्षया भूमिर्दोग्ध्री कामाननुत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Of all gifts, the gift of land is said to surpass them; for the unmoving, imperishable earth yields the best of wishes."}},{"n":3,"text":"दोग्ध्री वासांसि रत्नानि पशून्व्रीहियवांस्तथा ।\nभूमिदः सर्वभूतेषु शाश्वतीरेधते समाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She yields clothing, jewels, cattle, rice and barley; the giver of land prospers among all beings for endless years."}},{"n":4,"text":"यावद्भूमेरायुरिह तावद्भूमिद एधते ।\nन भूमिदानादस्तीह परं किंचिद्युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"As long as the earth lasts here, the giver of land prospers; there is nothing higher here than the gift of land, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":5,"text":"अप्यल्पं प्रददुः पूर्वे पृथिव्या इति नः श्रुतम् ।\nभूमिमेते ददुः सर्वे ये भूमिं भुञ्जते जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard that men of old gave even a small piece of the earth; all those who enjoy the land in effect gave land."}},{"n":6,"text":"स्वकर्मैवोपजीवन्ति नरा इह परत्र च ।\nभूमिर्भूतिर्महादेवी दातारं कुरुते प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"People live by their own deeds here and hereafter; the great goddess Earth, Prosperity, makes her giver beloved."}},{"n":7,"text":"य एतां दक्षिणां दद्यादक्षयां पृथिवीपतिः ।\nपुनर्नरत्वं संप्राप्य भवेत्स पृथिवीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who gives this imperishable fee will, regaining a human birth, again become a lord of the earth."}},{"n":8,"text":"यथा दानं तथा भोग इति धर्मेषु निश्चयः ।\nसंग्रामे वा तनुं जह्याद्दद्याद्वा पृथिवीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'As the gift, so the enjoyment' is the settled rule among duties; whether one gives up one's body in battle or gives this earth."}},{"n":9,"text":"इत्येतां क्षत्रबन्धूनां वदन्ति परमाशिषम् ।\nपुनाति दत्ता पृथिवी दातारमिति शुश्रुम ॥","meaning":{"en":"This, they say, is the highest blessing for the warrior class; we have heard that land given purifies the giver."}},{"n":10,"text":"अपि पापसमाचारं ब्रह्मघ्नमपि वानृतम् ।\nसैव पापं पावयति सैव पापात्प्रमोचयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even one who acts sinfully, a killer of brahmins, or a liar: she alone purifies from sin and frees from sin."}},{"n":11,"text":"अपि पापकृतां राज्ञां प्रतिगृह्णन्ति साधवः ।\nपृथिवीं नान्यदिच्छन्ति पावनं जननी यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Good people accept her even from kings who do wrong; they desire nothing else as a purifier, as one does a mother."}},{"n":12,"text":"नामास्याः प्रियदत्तेति गुह्यं देव्याः सनातनम् ।\nदानं वाप्यथ वा ज्ञानं नाम्नोऽस्याः परमं प्रियम् ।\nतस्मात्प्राप्यैव पृथिवीं दद्याद्विप्राय पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The eternal secret name of the goddess is 'Dear-Given'; either gift or knowledge is most dear to that name; therefore, having gained the earth, a king should give it to a brahmin."}},{"n":13,"text":"नाभूमिपतिना भूमिरधिष्ठेया कथंचन ।\nन वा पात्रेण वा गूहेदन्तर्धानेन वा चरेत् ।\nये चान्ये भूमिमिच्छेयुः कुर्युरेवमसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Land should never be held by one who is not a landholder, nor hidden in a vessel, nor treated by concealment; and any others who wish for land should act likewise, without doubt."}},{"n":14,"text":"यः साधोर्भूमिमादत्ते न भूमिं विन्दते तु सः ।\nभूमिं तु दत्त्वा साधुभ्यो विन्दते भूमिमेव हि ।\nप्रेत्येह च स धर्मात्मा संप्राप्नोति महद्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who takes land from a good man does not gain land; but one who gives land to good people gains land, and that righteous man earns great fame here and hereafter."}},{"n":15,"text":"यस्य विप्रानुशासन्ति साधोर्भूमिं सदैव हि ।\nन तस्य शत्रवो राजन्प्रशासन्ति वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the good man for whom brahmins always hold land, his enemies do not rule the earth, king."}},{"n":16,"text":"यत्किंचित्पुरुषः पापं कुरुते वृत्तिकर्शितः ।\nअपि गोचर्ममात्रेण भूमिदानेन पूयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever sin a man commits, weakened in his livelihood, is cleansed by a gift of land, even if only the size of a cow's hide."}},{"n":17,"text":"येऽपि संकीर्णकर्माणो राजानो रौद्रकर्मिणः ।\nतेभ्यः पवित्रमाख्येयं भूमिदानमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For kings of mixed deeds and cruel deeds, the gift of land is to be named the supreme purifier."}},{"n":18,"text":"अल्पान्तरमिदं शश्वत्पुराणा मेनिरे जनाः ।\nयो यजेदश्वमेधेन दद्याद्वा साधवे महीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ancients always held there is little difference between one who performs the Ashvamedha and one who gives land to a good person."}},{"n":19,"text":"अपि चेत्सुकृतं कृत्वा शङ्केरन्नपि पण्डिताः ।\nअशक्यमेकमेवैतद्भूमिदानमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if the wise suspect that after doing good deeds something remains, this one gift of land is unsurpassed and impossible to equal."}},{"n":20,"text":"सुवर्णं रजतं वस्त्रं मणिमुक्तावसूनि च ।\nसर्वमेतन्महाप्राज्ञ ददाति वसुधां ददत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gold, silver, clothes, gems, pearls and wealth: all this, wise one, one gives by giving the earth."}},{"n":21,"text":"तपो यज्ञः श्रुतं शीलमलोभः सत्यसंधता ।\nगुरुदैवतपूजा च नातिवर्तन्ति भूमिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Austerity, sacrifice, learning, good conduct, freedom from greed, truthfulness and worship of elders and gods do not surpass the giver of land."}},{"n":22,"text":"भर्तुर्निःश्रेयसे युक्तास्त्यक्तात्मानो रणे हताः ।\nब्रह्मलोकगताः सिद्धा नातिक्रामन्ति भूमिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those devoted to their master's good, who gave up their lives and died in battle, and perfected beings who have gone to Brahma's world, do not surpass the giver of land."}},{"n":23,"text":"यथा जनित्री क्षीरेण स्वपुत्रं भरते सदा ।\nअनुगृह्णाति दातारं तथा सर्वरसैर्मही ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a mother always nourishes her son with milk, so the earth with all flavours favours the giver."}},{"n":24,"text":"मृत्योर्वै किंकरो दण्डस्तापो वह्नेः सुदारुणः ।\nघोराश्च वारुणाः पाशा नोपसर्पन्ति भूमिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Death's servant the rod, the terrible heat of fire, and the dreadful snares of Varuna do not approach the giver of land."}},{"n":25,"text":"पितॄंश्च पितृलोकस्थान्देवलोके च देवताः ।\nसंतर्पयति शान्तात्मा यो ददाति वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who gives the earth, tranquil in soul, satisfies the ancestors in the world of ancestors and the gods in the world of the gods."}},{"n":26,"text":"कृशाय म्रियमाणाय वृत्तिम्लानाय सीदते ।\nभूमिं वृत्तिकरीं दत्त्वा सत्री भवति मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By giving a livelihood-yielding plot of land to a thin, dying one, withered in his living and sinking, a man becomes the sponsor of a great alms-house."}},{"n":27,"text":"यथा धावति गौर्वत्सं क्षीरमभ्युत्सृजन्त्युत ।\nएवमेव महाभाग भूमिर्भवति भूमिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a cow runs to her calf and lets her milk flow, so, great one, the earth becomes to the giver of land."}},{"n":28,"text":"हलकृष्टां महीं दत्त्वा सबीजां सफलामपि ।\nउदीर्णं वापि शरणं तथा भवति कामदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given land ploughed, with seed and even crops, or a refuge to one in need, he becomes a granter of wishes."}},{"n":29,"text":"ब्राह्मणं वृत्तसंपन्नमाहिताग्निं शुचिव्रतम् ।\nनरः प्रतिग्राह्य महीं न याति यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who has accepted land from a brahmin of good conduct, who keeps the sacred fires and pure vows, does not go to Yama's house."}},{"n":30,"text":"यथा चन्द्रमसो वृद्धिरहन्यहनि जायते ।\nतथा भूमिकृतं दानं सस्ये सस्ये विवर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the moon grows day by day, so a gift made of land increases with each harvest."}},{"n":31,"text":"अत्र गाथा भूमिगीताः कीर्तयन्ति पुराविदः ।\nयाः श्रुत्वा जामदग्न्येन दत्ता भूः काश्यपाय वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this the ancients recite verses sung by the Earth, hearing which Jamadagni's son gave the land to Kashyapa."}},{"n":32,"text":"मामेवादत्त मां दत्त मां दत्त्वा मामवाप्स्यथ ।\nअस्मिँल्लोके परे चैव ततश्चाजनने पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Take me, give me, having given me you will obtain me, in this world and the next, and afterwards in birth again.'"}},{"n":33,"text":"य इमां व्याहृतिं वेद ब्राह्मणो ब्रह्मसंश्रितः ।\nश्राद्धस्य हूयमानस्य ब्रह्मभूयं स गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin who knows this utterance and is devoted to Brahma attains union with Brahma at a shraddha oblation."}},{"n":34,"text":"कृत्यानामभिशस्तानां दुरिष्टशमनं महत् ।\nप्रायश्चित्तमहं कृत्वा पुनात्युभयतो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of sinful deeds and curses, this is a great remedy for evil sacrifices; I perform this atonement, and it purifies ten generations on both sides."}},{"n":35,"text":"पुनाति य इदं वेद वेद चाहं तथैव च ।\nप्रकृतिः सर्वभूतानां भूमिर्वै शाश्वती मता ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who knows this purifies, and I too know it; the Earth is held the eternal nature of all beings."}},{"n":36,"text":"अभिषिच्यैव नृपतिं श्रावयेदिममागमम् ।\nयथा श्रुत्वा महीं दद्यान्नादद्यात्साधुतश्च ताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having consecrated a king, one should have him hear this tradition, so that having heard it he gives the land and does not take it from the good."}},{"n":37,"text":"सोऽयं कृत्स्नो ब्राह्मणार्थो राजार्थश्चाप्यसंशयम् ।\nराजा हि धर्मकुशलः प्रथमं भूतिलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this is for brahmins and for kings, without doubt; for a king skilled in dharma is the first sign of prosperity."}},{"n":38,"text":"अथ येषामधर्मज्ञो राजा भवति नास्तिकः ।\nन ते सुखं प्रबुध्यन्ते न सुखं प्रस्वपन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"But those whose king is ignorant of dharma and godless do not wake in comfort nor sleep in comfort."}},{"n":39,"text":"सदा भवन्ति चोद्विग्नास्तस्य दुश्चरितैर्नराः ।\nयोगक्षेमा हि बहवो राष्ट्रं नास्याविशन्ति तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men are always anxious through his misdeeds, and many people of secure welfare do not enter his kingdom."}},{"n":40,"text":"अथ येषां पुनः प्राज्ञो राजा भवति धार्मिकः ।\nसुखं ते प्रतिबुध्यन्ते सुसुखं प्रस्वपन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"But those whose king is wise and righteous wake happily and sleep very happily."}},{"n":41,"text":"तस्य राज्ञः शुभैरार्यैः कर्मभिर्निर्वृताः प्रजाः ।\nयोगक्षेमेण वृष्ट्या च विवर्धन्ते स्वकर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Contented by that king's good, noble deeds, his subjects prosper in security, rain and their own works."}},{"n":42,"text":"स कुलीनः स पुरुषः स बन्धुः स च पुण्यकृत् ।\nस दाता स च विक्रान्तो यो ददाति वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is well-born, he is a real man, he is a kinsman and a doer of merit, he is a giver and a hero, who gives the earth."}},{"n":43,"text":"आदित्या इव दीप्यन्ते तेजसा भुवि मानवाः ।\nददन्ति वसुधां स्फीतां ये वेदविदुषि द्विजे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men who give the broad earth to a brahmin learned in the Vedas shine on earth with splendour like the Adityas."}},{"n":44,"text":"यथा बीजानि रोहन्ति प्रकीर्णानि महीतले ।\nतथा कामाः प्ररोहन्ति भूमिदानसमार्जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As seeds sown on the ground sprout, so desires sprout that are earned by giving land."}},{"n":45,"text":"आदित्यो वरुणो विष्णुर्ब्रह्मा सोमो हुताशनः ।\nशूलपाणिश्च भगवान्प्रतिनन्दन्ति भूमिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Sun, Varuna, Vishnu, Brahma, Soma, Fire, and the lord who holds the trident are pleased with the giver of land."}},{"n":46,"text":"भूमौ जायन्ति पुरुषा भूमौ निष्ठां व्रजन्ति च ।\nचतुर्विधो हि लोकोऽयं योऽयं भूमिगुणात्मकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men are born on earth and end on earth; for this fourfold world is made of the earth's quality."}},{"n":47,"text":"एषा माता पिता चैव जगतः पृथिवीपते ।\nनानया सदृशं भूतं किंचिदस्ति जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"She is mother and father of the world, lord of the earth; nothing is like her, lord of men."}},{"n":48,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nबृहस्पतेश्च संवादमिन्द्रस्य च युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this they also tell this ancient story, the dialogue of Brihaspati and Indra, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":49,"text":"इष्ट्वा क्रतुशतेनाथ महता दक्षिणावता ।\nमघवा वाग्विदां श्रेष्ठं पप्रच्छेदं बृहस्पतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having performed a hundred great sacrifices with fees, Indra asked this of Brihaspati, best of speakers."}},{"n":50,"text":"भगवन्केन दानेन स्वर्गतः सुखमेधते ।\nयदक्षयं महार्घं च तद्ब्रूहि वदतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Lord, by what gift does one prosper happily in heaven? Tell me what is imperishable and most precious, best of speakers.'"}},{"n":51,"text":"इत्युक्तः स सुरेन्द्रेण ततो देवपुरोहितः ।\nबृहस्पतिर्महातेजाः प्रत्युवाच शतक्रतुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed by the lord of the gods, Brihaspati, the gods' priest, of great splendour, answered Indra."}},{"n":52,"text":"सुवर्णदानं गोदानं भूमिदानं च वृत्रहन् ।\nदददेतान्महाप्राज्ञः सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Gifts of gold, cows and land, slayer of Vritra: the wise one who gives these is freed from all sins."}},{"n":53,"text":"न भूमिदानाद्देवेन्द्र परं किंचिदिति प्रभो ।\nविशिष्टमिति मन्यामि यथा प्राहुर्मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is nothing higher than the gift of land, lord of the gods; I consider it the best, as the wise say."}},{"n":54,"text":"ये शूरा निहता युद्धे स्वर्याता दानगृद्धिनः ।\nसर्वे ते विबुधश्रेष्ठ नातिक्रामन्ति भूमिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The heroes killed in battle who went to heaven, eager to give, all of them, best of gods, do not surpass the giver of land."}},{"n":55,"text":"भर्तुर्निःश्रेयसे युक्तास्त्यक्तात्मानो रणे हताः ।\nब्रह्मलोकगताः शूरा नातिक्रामन्ति भूमिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those devoted to their master's good who gave up their lives in battle and went to Brahma's world do not surpass the giver of land."}},{"n":56,"text":"पञ्च पूर्वादिपुरुषाः षट्च ये वसुधां गताः ।\nएकादश ददद्भूमिं परित्रातीह मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Five ancestors, six who went to the earth, eleven in all: the man who gives land rescues them here."}},{"n":57,"text":"रत्नोपकीर्णां वसुधां यो ददाति पुरंदर ।\nस मुक्तः सर्वकलुषैः स्वर्गलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who gives the earth strewn with jewels, Indra, is freed from all stains and honoured in heaven."}},{"n":58,"text":"महीं स्फीतां ददद्राजा सर्वकामगुणान्विताम् ।\nराजाधिराजो भवति तद्धि दानमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who gives the broad earth, endowed with all desired qualities, becomes king of kings; that gift is unsurpassed."}},{"n":59,"text":"सर्वकामसमायुक्तां काश्यपीं यः प्रयच्छति ।\nसर्वभूतानि मन्यन्ते मां ददातीति वासव ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who gives Kashyapi, the earth, furnished with all desires, all beings think, Vasava, 'He gives me.'"}},{"n":60,"text":"सर्वकामदुघां धेनुं सर्वकामपुरोगमाम् ।\nददाति यः सहस्राक्ष स स्वर्गं याति मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who gives, thousand-eyed one, a cow yielding all desires, preceded by all desires, goes to heaven."}},{"n":61,"text":"मधुसर्पिःप्रवाहिन्यः पयोदधिवहास्तथा ।\nसरितस्तर्पयन्तीह सुरेन्द्र वसुधाप्रदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rivers flowing with honey and ghee, milk and curds, satisfy here the giver of land, lord of gods."}},{"n":62,"text":"भूमिप्रदानान्नृपतिर्मुच्यते राजकिल्बिषात् ।\nन हि भूमिप्रदानेन दानमन्यद्विशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through the gift of land a king is freed from the king's sins; no other gift surpasses the gift of land."}},{"n":63,"text":"ददाति यः समुद्रान्तां पृथिवीं शस्त्रनिर्जिताम् ।\nतं जनाः कथयन्तीह यावद्धरति गौरियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives the earth ringed by oceans, won by weapons, people speak of as long as this earth sustains."}},{"n":64,"text":"पुण्यामृद्धरसां भूमिं यो ददाति पुरंदर ।\nन तस्य लोकाः क्षीयन्ते भूमिदानगुणार्जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who gives holy land rich in juices, Indra, his worlds earned by the virtue of the gift of land are not exhausted."}},{"n":65,"text":"सर्वथा पार्थिवेनेह सततं भूतिमिच्छता ।\nभूर्देया विधिवच्छक्र पात्रे सुखमभीप्सता ॥","meaning":{"en":"In every way, Shakra, a king who wishes always for prosperity and for happiness should give land to a worthy person by rule."}},{"n":66,"text":"अपि कृत्वा नरः पापं भूमिं दत्त्वा द्विजातये ।\nसमुत्सृजति तत्पापं जीर्णां त्वचमिवोरगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even after doing sin, a man who has given land to a brahmin sheds that sin as a snake sheds its old skin."}},{"n":67,"text":"सागरान्सरितः शैलान्काननानि च सर्वशः ।\nसर्वमेतन्नरः शक्र ददाति वसुधां ददत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Oceans, rivers, mountains and forests everywhere: all this, Shakra, a man gives by giving the earth."}},{"n":68,"text":"तडागान्युदपानानि स्रोतांसि च सरांसि च ।\nस्नेहान्सर्वरसांश्चैव ददाति वसुधां ददत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tanks, wells, streams and lakes, oils and all flavours, one gives by giving the earth."}},{"n":69,"text":"ओषधीः क्षीरसंपन्ना नगान्पुष्पफलान्वितान् ।\nकाननोपलशैलांश्च ददाति वसुधां ददत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Plants rich in milk, trees with flowers and fruit, forests, rocks and hills, one gives by giving the earth."}},{"n":70,"text":"अग्निष्टोमप्रभृतिभिरिष्ट्वा च स्वाप्तदक्षिणैः ।\nन तत्फलमवाप्नोति भूमिदानाद्यदश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having sacrificed with the Agnishtoma and others with fine fees, one does not obtain the fruit that one gets from the gift of land."}},{"n":71,"text":"दाता दशानुगृह्णाति दश हन्ति तथा क्षिपन् ।\nपूर्वदत्तां हरन्भूमिं नरकायोपगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The giver blesses ten and one who casts it off strikes ten; one who takes back land given before goes to hell."}},{"n":72,"text":"न ददाति प्रतिश्रुत्य दत्त्वा वा हरते तु यः ।\nस बद्धो वारुणैः पाशैस्तप्यते मृत्युशासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who does not give after promising, or takes back after giving, is bound by Varuna's snares and tormented by Death's rule."}},{"n":73,"text":"आहिताग्निं सदायज्ञं कृशभृत्यं प्रियातिथिम् ।\nये भरन्ति द्विजश्रेष्ठं नोपसर्पन्ति ते यमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who support the best of brahmins who keeps the fire, is always sacrificing, has few servants, and loves guests, do not approach Yama."}},{"n":74,"text":"ब्राह्मणेष्वृणभूतं स्यात्पार्थिवस्य पुरंदर ।\nइतरेषां तु वर्णानां तारयेत्कृशदुर्बलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a king, a brahmin is as if a debt; but he should rescue the thin and weak among other classes."}},{"n":75,"text":"नाच्छिन्द्यात्स्पर्शितां भूमिं परेण त्रिदशाधिप ।\nब्राह्मणाय सुरश्रेष्ठ कृशभृत्याय कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one, lord of the thirty gods, should seize land once granted to a brahmin of few attendants by another, best of gods."}},{"n":76,"text":"अथाश्रु पतितं तेषां दीनानामवसीदताम् ।\nब्राह्मणानां हृते क्षेत्रे हन्यात्त्रिपुरुषं कुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The tears that fall from those poor, afflicted brahmins, when their field is taken, destroy the family for three generations."}},{"n":77,"text":"भूमिपालं च्युतं राष्ट्राद्यस्तु संस्थापयेत्पुनः ।\nतस्य वासः सहस्राक्ष नाकपृष्ठे महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who restores to his kingdom a king who has fallen from it, thousand-eyed one, is honoured in heaven's vault."}},{"n":78,"text":"इक्षुभिः संततां भूमिं यवगोधूमसंकुलाम् ।\nगोश्ववाहनसंपूर्णां बाहुवीर्यसमार्जिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives land abounding in sugar cane, crowded with barley and wheat, full of cattle, horses and vehicles, earned by the strength of his arms,"}},{"n":79,"text":"निधिगर्भां ददद्भूमिं सर्वरत्नपरिच्छदाम् ।\nअक्षयाँल्लभते लोकान्भूमिसत्रं हि तस्य तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"holding treasure, with all gems as equipment, gains imperishable worlds, for that is his land sacrifice."}},{"n":80,"text":"विधूय कलुषं सर्वं विरजाः संमतः सताम् ।\nलोके महीयते सद्भिर्यो ददाति वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaking off all stain, free from dust, esteemed by the good, he who gives the earth is honoured in the world by the good."}},{"n":81,"text":"यथाप्सु पतितः शक्र तैलबिन्दुर्विसर्पति ।\nतथा भूमिकृतं दानं सस्ये सस्ये विसर्पति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a drop of oil falling on water spreads, Shakra, so a gift made of land spreads with each harvest."}},{"n":82,"text":"ये रणाग्रे महीपालाः शूराः समितिशोभनाः ।\nवध्यन्तेऽभिमुखाः शक्र ब्रह्मलोकं व्रजन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings who are heroes at the head of battle, ornaments of assemblies, who are killed facing the enemy, go to the world of Brahma, Shakra."}},{"n":83,"text":"नृत्यगीतपरा नार्यो दिव्यमाल्यविभूषिताः ।\nउपतिष्ठन्ति देवेन्द्र सदा भूमिप्रदं दिवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Women devoted to dance and song, adorned with divine garlands, always attend the giver of land in heaven, lord of gods."}},{"n":84,"text":"मोदते च सुखं स्वर्गे देवगन्धर्वपूजितः ।\nयो ददाति महीं सम्यग्विधिनेह द्विजातये ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who gives land properly by rule here to a brahmin rejoices happily in heaven, honoured by gods and gandharvas."}},{"n":85,"text":"शतमप्सरसश्चैव दिव्यमाल्यविभूषिताः ।\nउपतिष्ठन्ति देवेन्द्र सदा भूमिप्रदं नरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A hundred apsaras adorned with divine garlands always attend the man who gives land, lord of gods."}},{"n":86,"text":"शङ्खं भद्रासनं छत्रं वराश्वा वरवारणाः ।\nभूमिप्रदानात्पुष्पाणि हिरण्यनिचयास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A conch, a throne, an umbrella, the best horses and best elephants, flowers and heaps of gold come from giving land."}},{"n":87,"text":"आज्ञा सदाप्रतिहता जयशब्दो भवत्यथ ।\nभूमिदानस्य पुष्पाणि फलं स्वर्गः पुरंदर ॥","meaning":{"en":"His command is never obstructed, and shouts of victory arise; these are the flowers of the gift of land, Purandara, and its fruit is heaven."}},{"n":88,"text":"हिरण्यपुष्पाश्चौषध्यः कुशकाञ्चनशाड्वलाः ।\nअमृतप्रसवां भूमिं प्राप्नोति पुरुषो ददत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The giver obtains the earth giving birth to nectar, with plants having golden flowers, kusha grass, gold and fresh grass."}},{"n":89,"text":"नास्ति भूमिसमं दानं नास्ति मातृसमो गुरुः ।\nनास्ति सत्यसमो धर्मो नास्ति दानसमो निधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No gift equals a gift of land, no teacher equals the mother, no duty equals truth, no treasure equals giving.'"}},{"n":90,"text":"एतदाङ्गिरसाच्छ्रुत्वा वासवो वसुधामिमाम् ।\nवसुरत्नसमाकीर्णां ददावाङ्गिरसे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this from Angirasa's descendant, Vasava then gave this earth, strewn with wealth and jewels, to him."}},{"n":91,"text":"य इमं श्रावयेच्छ्राद्धे भूमिदानस्य संस्तवम् ।\nन तस्य रक्षसां भागो नासुराणां भवत्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who recites this praise of the gift of land at a shraddha has no portion for demons or for asuras."}},{"n":92,"text":"अक्षयं च भवेद्दत्तं पितृभ्यस्तन्न संशयः ।\nतस्माच्छ्राद्धेष्विदं विप्रो भुञ्जतः श्रावयेद्द्विजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What he gives to the ancestors becomes imperishable, without doubt; therefore a brahmin should recite this to the twice-born who are eating at shraddhas."}},{"n":93,"text":"इत्येतत्सर्वदानानां श्रेष्ठमुक्तं तवानघ ।\nमया भरतशार्दूल किं भूयः श्रोतुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"This, blameless one, I have said to be the best of all gifts, tiger of the Bharatas; what more do you wish to hear?\""}}]}]}